# Build context is the repo root. deploy/Dockerfile copies five named paths (package.json, bun.lock, packages/,
# server/, web/); this file is the second line of defence: it filters inside those paths and keeps the context small.
# Docker matches these against the context root: unlike .gitignore, a bare `*.db` only matches at the top
# level, so patterns that must match at any depth start with `**/`.

# Repo history, CI, docs and agent notes: not needed to run the server.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
docs
CLAUDE.md
README.md
PROTOCOL.md
.rig
.code-foundations

# Packaging files. Docker reads deploy/Dockerfile itself; nothing in deploy/ is used at runtime.
# This also keeps deploy/.env (where Compose reads secrets) out of the image.
deploy

# Tests run in CI from a checkout, not from the image; test/ holds fakes (a fake identity provider, a fake
# store) that should not ship. Nothing in server/, web/ or packages/ imports from test/.
test

# Design notes and dev/CI scripts (rig, clean, test-cluster): not part of the running server.
design
scripts

# Dependencies are installed inside the image from bun.lock (`bun install --frozen-lockfile --production`), never
# copied from the host. bun.lock itself must stay in the context: never list it here.
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets, at any depth. No exception for .env.example: the image does not need the template.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/client_secret*.json
**/.envrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*credentials*.json

# Local databases (SQLite and its sidecar files), at any depth.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-wal
**/*.sqlite3-shm
**/*.sqlite3-journal

# Local data and blob directories at the repo root (the container uses /data on a volume).
data
blobs
